# Elixser Peptides — Project Rules
# Next.js 14 + TypeScript + Tailwind + WooCommerce Headless

# ═════════════════════════════════════════════
# SECTION 0: HARD RULES — read first, no exceptions
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════

## 0.1 NEVER place a Tagada order

  The user places every Tagada order themselves, by hand. Never complete one.

  NOT ALLOWED:
  - Clicking "Complete Purchase" / "Pay" on a Tagada hosted checkout page
  - Submitting payment details, card numbers or test cards anywhere on Tagada
  - Any step whose next click would create an order

  ALLOWED (needed to build and debug):
  - The tracker's session calls (/session/anonymous, /session/v2/init, /funnel/initialize)
  - /funnel/navigate — this returns a checkout URL, it does not create an order
  - Opening that checkout URL and READING the page to verify products and totals

  If a check cannot be done without ordering, stop and hand it to the user with
  the exact steps instead of doing it.

## 0.2 Internal / instruction files NEVER go to git

  The client does not need our working docs. Anything you create that is an
  instruction, guide, report, context note, or backend hand-off (PDF, DOC/DOCX,
  MD, HTML export, ZIP, plugin zips, etc.) is for us only.

  RULE: the moment you create such a file, add it to .gitignore in the SAME step
  (exact filename, under "Internal working docs"). Never commit or stage it.

  Examples: *-CONTEXT.md, *-BACKEND.md, *-REPORT.*, testing-instructions.pdf,
  Website_Issues_and_Fixes.pdf, /backend, /docs, local backup zips.
  Real source code (src/, public/) is the only thing that gets committed.

