## G1. Color Tokens — use these exact values, no hardcoding elsewhere

  /* Brand */
  --color-blue:          #0165FF   /* primary brand blue — announcement bar, links, accents */
  --color-blue-alt:      #3473FB   /* slightly lighter blue — some hover states */
  --color-blue-bg:       #F5F8FF   /* light blue tint — subtle section backgrounds */

  /* Text */
  --color-ink:           #1A1A1A   /* primary body text */
  --color-ink-dark:      #0A0A0A   /* headings, product titles, dark CTAs */
  --color-black:         #000000   /* pure black — hero CTA button bg */
  --color-muted:         #8A8A85   /* secondary / helper text */
  --color-muted-alt:     #707070   /* --c-light in original — captions, meta */

  /* Surfaces */
  --color-white:         #FFFFFF   /* default page background, cards */
  --color-cream:         #F5F5F2   /* off-white — subtle section bg, age gate dark surface */
  --color-gray-light:    #EEEEEE   /* dividers, borders */
  --color-dark:          #111111   /* dark section backgrounds */
  --color-dark-alt:      #0A0A0A   /* near-black — nav bar, CTA button */

  /* Accent */
  --color-star:          #CCA43B   /* star / gold rating color */
  --color-green-bg:      #E9F9F0   /* light green tint — success / badge bg */

  RULE: Define all of these in src/app/globals.css as :root CSS variables.
        In Tailwind config, extend colors to reference these vars.
        Never use a hex code directly in a component — always use the token name.

