## K1. Backend — Elixser Loyalty API plugin

  FILE:    backend/elixser-loyalty-api.zip  (already uploaded live to new2.elixserpeptides.com)
  PLUGIN:  "Elixser Loyalty API" — custom WP plugin wrapping WPLoyalty REST routes
  SECRET:  ELX_LOYALTY_SECRET in .env.local must match ELX_LOYALTY_SECRET in wp-config.php
           Currently empty in .env.local — fill it in or the X-Elx-Loyalty-Secret header is blank
  BASE URL: {NEXT_PUBLIC_WP_URL}/wp-json/elx/v1/loyalty

  ENDPOINTS (all need Bearer authToken OR email+secret):
    GET  /me                          → LoyaltySummary (points, tier, rewards, referral, waysToEarn, settings)
    GET  /history?page=&per_page=     → LoyaltyHistory (activity log)
    GET  /coupons?type=active|expired → LoyaltyCoupons (claimed coupon codes)
    POST /redeem                      → body: { reward_id, reward_table, points } → LoyaltyActionResult
    POST /settings                    → body: { email_opt_in, birthday, campaign_id }
    GET  /product-points?product_id=  → LoyaltyProductPoints (for product page earn line)
    GET  /cart-points                 → LoyaltyCartPoints (for cart banner)

## K2. Next.js files

  src/lib/loyalty.ts                          → all calls to the plugin (server-only)
  src/types/loyalty.ts                        → all TypeScript interfaces
  src/app/account/points/page.tsx             → server page: calls API in parallel, passes to client
  src/components/loyalty/PointsPageClient.tsx → main client component with tabs + redeem logic
  src/components/loyalty/LoyaltySection.tsx   → shared section heading wrapper
  src/components/loyalty/PointsCards.tsx      → MY POINTS: 3 stat cards (Available, Redeemed, Used)
  src/components/loyalty/LevelProgress.tsx    → MY LEVELS: progress bar with tier names + gap text
  src/components/loyalty/ReferralLink.tsx     → REFERRAL LINK: copy-to-clipboard input
  src/components/loyalty/RewardCard.tsx       → REWARDS tab: catalogue item with "Redeem Now" button
  src/components/loyalty/CouponCard.tsx       → COUPONS tab: claimed coupon + "Apply Coupon" button
  src/components/loyalty/RecentActivities.tsx → RECENT ACTIVITIES: table of point history
  src/components/loyalty/WaysToEarnCard.tsx   → WAYS TO EARN: campaign card grid (icon by actionType)
  src/components/loyalty/RewardIcon.tsx       → SVG coin-in-hand icon used on reward/coupon cards
  src/app/api/loyalty/redeem/route.ts         → POST — adds authToken server-side then calls plugin
  src/app/api/loyalty/settings/route.ts       → POST — saves email opt-in / birthday

## K3. Page sections (order matches the live WP widget)

  1. MY POINTS        — 3 cards: Available Points, Redeemed Points, Used Rewards (with USD select)
  2. MY LEVELS        — progress bar: current tier → next tier, gap sentence, 0–1000 axis
  3. REFERRAL LINK    — read-only input with Copy Link button
  4. MY REWARDS       — 3 tabs: Rewards | Coupons | Used & Expired Coupons
  5. RECENT ACTIVITIES — table: Order No. / Action Type / Message / Points / Rewards
  6. WAYS TO EARN REWARDS — grid of campaign cards, icon mapped from actionType
  7. NOTIFICATION PREFERENCE — single checkbox: opt-in for points & rewards emails

## K4. Redeem flow

  - User clicks "Redeem Now" on a RewardCard
  - POST /api/loyalty/redeem → WordPress creates WC coupon, returns { points, code }
  - Client updates local points balance, switches tab to "Coupons"
  - Page reloads to fetch the fresh coupon from the server

## K5. Rules

  - Never calculate points in Next.js — WordPress does all maths (WPLoyalty plugin)
  - Never show 0 as balance if the API call failed — show a "not available" notice instead
  - The loyalty API secret (ELX_LOYALTY_SECRET) is server-only — never NEXT_PUBLIC_
  - Product earn line lives in src/components/product/EarnPointsLine.tsx (already exists)
  - Cart banner lives in src/components/cart/LoyaltyBanner.tsx (already exists)

## K6. Auth fix (session 2026-10-06)

  FILE: src/lib/auth.ts  function getAuthToken()
  CHANGE: when refreshAuthToken() throws (network error / timeout), return null instead of
          throwing BackendUnreachableError. This shows the login form instead of the error boundary.
  FILE: src/lib/refreshToken.ts
  CHANGE: non-200 HTTP response from the JWT refresh endpoint now returns null (signed-out)
          instead of throwing, so a 401/403 from WP doesn't look like "backend down".

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECTION L: PRODUCT REVIEWS (WiserReview)  ✅ BUILT (needs the plugin uploaded to WordPress)
# WiserReview saves each product's rating + reviews in post meta `wiserrw_schema_json`.
# We read that through our own endpoint — we never load WiserReview's widget script.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

## L1. Backend — Elixser Reviews API plugin  (documented per A8)

  FILE:     backend/elixser-reviews-api.zip   (upload: WP Admin → Plugins → Add New → Upload)
  NEEDS:    WiserReview plugin active, API key connected, Sync Products run once
  ENDPOINT: GET {NEXT_PUBLIC_WP_URL}/wp-json/elx/v1/reviews?product_ids=12,34   (public, max 20 ids)
  REPLIES:  { "12": { rating, count, reviews:[{author, body, rating}], writeReviewUrl } }
  NOTE:     `reviews` holds only the reviews WiserReview put in its schema (first few), `count` is the real total.
            No review date is sent — the schema does not carry one.

## L2. Next.js files

  src/types/review.ts                       → ProductReview, ProductReviews
  src/lib/reviews.ts                        → the only fetch to the plugin (server-only, ISR 1 hour, tag "reviews")
  src/lib/reviewFormat.ts                   → count label + the rating line under the title
  src/lib/reviewSchema.ts                   → JSON-LD for Google stars (null when 0 reviews)
  src/components/product/ReviewsSection.tsx → section shell + empty / "not available" states
  src/components/product/ReviewsSummary.tsx → "4.5 ★★★★★ (3 reviews)"
  src/components/product/ReviewCard.tsx     → one review
  src/components/product/StarRow.tsx        → shared stars (title rating + review cards)
  src/components/product/WriteReviewButton.tsx → opens the hosted WiserReview form in a new tab
  src/components/product/ReviewJsonLd.tsx   → prints the JSON-LD script

## L3. Rules

  - Plugin unreachable → reviews = null → show "not available", never a false "no reviews yet".
  - 0 reviews → the title rating keeps the old RATING default (productDefaults.ts); JSON-LD is skipped.
  - Never calculate ratings in Next.js — WiserReview/WordPress own the numbers.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECTION M: CONTACT FORM (Contact Form 7 + Flamingo)  ✅ BUILT
# /contact form → Next.js server action → Contact Form 7 REST → mail + saved in Flamingo
# No custom WordPress plugin, so nothing new to document under A8.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

## M1. Backend (WordPress, new2.elixserpeptides.com)

  PLUGINS:  Contact Form 7 + Flamingo (Flamingo keeps every message: WP Admin → Flamingo → Inbound Messages)
  FORM ID:  8764  (CF7_CONTACT_FORM_ID in .env.local — set it in Vercel/hosting env too)
  FIELDS:   your-name, your-email, your-phone, your-message  (names must match src/lib/contactApi.ts)
  MAIL:     set in the form's Mail tab (To, Reply-To [your-email]). Use an SMTP plugin on the live site.
  ENDPOINT: POST {NEXT_PUBLIC_WP_URL}/wp-json/contact-form-7/v1/contact-forms/8764/feedback  (multipart, public)

## M2. Next.js files

  src/types/contactForm.ts                  → ContactFormValues, ContactFormState, Cf7FeedbackResponse
  src/lib/contactApi.ts                     → the only fetch to Contact Form 7 (server-only)
  src/actions/contact.ts                    → validates, bot trap, calls contactApi
  src/components/contact/ContactForm.tsx    → form state + submit
  src/components/contact/ContactSubmit.tsx  → button with "Sending…" + Spinner
  src/components/contact/ContactStatus.tsx  → thank-you / error line

## M3. Rules

  - CF7 answers HTTP 200 even on failure — only status "mail_sent" means it worked.
  - Submit through startTransition, never <form action> (React 19 blanks the fields — see J3).
  - Hidden field `website` is the bot trap: filled = pretend success, send nothing.
  - Renaming a field in the CF7 form breaks the mapping in contactApi.ts — change both together.
